                "mimeType": "image/png",
                "width": 1536,
                "height": 1024,
                "alt": "A cathedral-sized whale fashioned from smoky volcanic glass lies across a copper-coloured mountain terrace. Its hollow ribs cast amber patterns on the ground; the rising tail is visible from distant carrying paths. Assayers and guides work beside the jaw, while the brittle interior remains outside the ordinary visitor route. Tool marks and joined ribs identify it as a crafted structure, though its makers' intended meaning is disputed.",
